##
    A project that lists two programs, both in the same place.

    Neither file writes a namespace, so both Programs are the same name, and two types cannot
    share one. That is what is reported here, and it has nothing to do with entry points: the
    same error would come of two models called Shape.

    Two Programs in different namespaces are two different types and are allowed. Something
    must then say which one begins, and the project says it with an 'entry' line — see
    ambiguous-entry.pcp beside this one.

    The folder rule never runs into either case, since it takes only the program that was named
    and the shared code beside it. A project has to be told.
##

project TwoPrograms
    source ../runtime/divide-by-zero.pc
    source ../runtime/index-out-of-range.pc
end project
